== 3. verdict ==
  The migration RAISED against already-current data.
  -> a fresh deployment cannot simply run the full history; it needs baselining,
     and Beanie provides no --fake/--stamp flag to do it.


CLI SURFACE, for the record -- `beanie migrate --help`:
  --forward / --backward
  -d, --distance TEXT              0 = all the migrations. Default is 0
  -uri, --connection-uri TEXT
  -db, --database_name TEXT
  -p, --path TEXT
  --allow-index-dropping / --forbid-index-dropping
  --use-transaction / --no-use-transaction
        "When enabled, Beanie uses transactions for migration, which
         necessitates a replica set."

There is NO --fake, --stamp or baseline option. The only skip mechanism in the
source is runner.py:207, "Skip migrations that start with an underscore" -- which
is global to the migrations directory, not per environment, so it cannot baseline
one database while leaving others to migrate.
